comments.message:
Although I would also prefer that it is immutable, the motivation for a setter is an issue of scope. I need to set the I2CBus value differently based on whether we are using the "Bus" or "MuxChannel" to configure it in EM. Afterwards I2CBus is used to create the sensor (see https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/75503 for context/examples).
Currently, it is set up as the following:

```
...
I2CBus bus;
...

if ("Bus" keyword used)
{
    bus.setBus(busNumber)
}
else if ("MuxChannel" interface used)
{
    ...
    bus = mux.getLogicalBus(channelName)
    ...
}

XSensor(bus, addr, ...)
```

Isn't that rather a matter of only instantiating a I2CBus instance if the `Bus` keyword is used?

```
if ("Bus" keyword used)
{
    bus = I2CBus(... busNumber ...);
}
else if ("MuxChannel" interface used)
{
    ...
    bus = mux.getLogicalBus(channelName);
    ...
}
```
